      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface display confirmed by anti-HA immunostaining of intact (non-permeabilized) MDCK cells (L2, L3). Folding and function explicitly stated to be unaffected: 'previously shown to have no effect on normal folding and function of kAE1' (L1); 'integration of an epitope tag into the third extracellular loop affect neither kAE1 function nor its correct localization in mammalian cells' (L7).",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L4 explicitly names the junction as 'between Asn556 and Val557', confirmed by Python: seq[555]='N' (Asn556) and seq[556]='V' (Val557), both within EC3 (542\u2013569). The insert sits 15 residues from the upstream TM boundary (TM5 ends at 541) and 13 residues from the downstream TM boundary (TM6 starts at 570), well beyond the \u22653 residue minimum. No cysteines or NxS/T glycosylation sequons are present in EC3. Independent validation across at least four publications (PMC3584104, PMC6992373, PMC9623938, PMC12959882) with both HA and Myc tags, and explicit functional assays, makes this a high-confidence site. Full-length kAE1 (kidney isoform of SLC4A1) expressed in MDCK cells and yeast with an HA epitope tag inserted between Asn556 and Val557 in the third extracellular loop (EC3, residues 542\u2013569, eAE1 canonical numbering). L4 (PMC6992373) is the most precise pinning: 'HA tag within the third extracellular loop between Asn556 and Val557'. Multiple independent papers (PMC3584104, PMC9623938, PMC12959882) corroborate the same position as 'position 557' in the same loop. A Myc tag at the same position is reported in PMC9623938 (L8).",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 31996424,
          "citation": "PMID 31996424",
          "claim": "(C and D) Western blot analysis of yeast cells expressing yeast codon-optimized variants of untagged wild-type kAE1 (kAE1 WT ), kAE1 containing an HA tag within the third extracellular loop between Asn 556 and Val 557 (kAE1 HA ), truncated kAE1 (kAE1 B3Mem ) (C), or kAE1 with an N-terminal fusion to yeast enhanced GFP (yeGFP-kAE1) (D)."
