  "literature_notes": "All nine ledger lines (L1\u2013L9) converge on a single surface site: the HA or Myc epitope tag in the third extracellular loop of SLC4A1 at the junction between residues 556 and 557 (eAE1/canonical UniProt numbering). L4 provides the most precise residue-level pinning ('between Asn556 and Val557'); L1, L2, L3, L8, and L9 describe the same position as 'at position 557', consistent with insert_after_residue=556. L5 states 'between aa 557 and 578', but residue 578 falls within TM6 (570\u2013588); this is interpreted as a loose description of the same loop insertion, not a distinct junction at 578. L6 and L7 provide functional validation without adding a new position. No ledger line supports any insertion in EC1 (426\u2013439), EC2 (472\u2013486), EC4 (625\u2013660), or the single-residue EC5/EC6/EC7 spans. The C-terminal HA tag mentioned in L8 is intracellular and is recorded in other_positions.",
